      "value": "instead of splitting world files i suggest a option to get the world data files stored in VRChats own streaming assets files so unity can render the worlds locally (caching works a bit but causes way more issues because of how the files are re-encoded and split) and only have to download avatars (rather have a map download 1 time for 5 minutes and then 20 seconds afterwards then risk infinite loops because a single file part fails to download due to server overload)",
