  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A current problem with worlds is that everything in the world needs to be included in the same file. This problem causes long downloading and updating of worlds with huge or a large number objects.\n\nSimilar to how avatars are loaded into a world, I'm suggesting splitting worlds into multiple files by added a way to create, upload and link \"world prefabs\" into a world.\n\nThis feature could also be integrated with triggers to control the loading and unloading of these prefabs. Imagine a puzzle world where each step is different file that is downloaded or a large scale world split onto different areas and downloaded when you move between them. Separating world object into different files can improve the performance, increase user interaction with less time transitioning between worlds and greatly speed up the updating and collaboration process for authors.",
